kb:source-subscription rdf:type ktype:Feature ;
               rdfs:label   "Source Subscription" ;
               kpred:has-status   "planned" ;
               kpred:description  "Mark a URL source as recurring with a check interval. Auto-creates dated source records." ;
               kpred:relates-to   kb:source-discovery ;
               kpred:relates-to   kb:source-reference-copy ;
               kpred:decided      "THIS IS THE PROMOTION TARGET FOR DISCOVERY, AND THE MOMENT A ONE-OFF BECOMES AN OBLIGATION (2026-07-31, expanding a one-line stub). Subscribing is the deliberate act F123 hands off to: a source found by a one-time search becomes a recurring commitment only when the user says so. Each refresh then runs the F122 gate ladder against the retained reviewed copy rather than re-extracting, so a subscription to a quiet site costs a conditional request and nothing else. What is missing beyond the interval is the exit: an UNSUBSCRIBE that is as easy as the subscribe, and a way to see what a subscription has actually contributed, since a source that has produced nothing but triage for a month is one the user should be told about rather than left paying for." .

