               kpred:decided      "SCOPE IS THE SAFETY BOUNDARY, and it is Matt's explicit constraint (2026-07-31): writes are restricted to directories the user has EXPLICITLY SYNCED. The app may create or edit inside a linked folder and nowhere else in the user's Drive. This must be enforced in code and tested — an assistant with unscoped write access to someone's entire Drive is a different and much worse product than one that owns a folder. A path check that can be bypassed by a `../` or by a file id resolved outside the folder tree is not a boundary." ;
               kpred:remaining    "Drive files.create / files.update behind the existing OAuth; a folder-scope guard resolving every target's PARENT CHAIN (an id-based API means path strings are not enough); graph node <-> Drive file identity so an edit updates rather than duplicates; conflict handling shared with the folder-sync reconcile." .

