               kpred:honest-note  "THE REASON THIS FEATURE EXISTS IS A MEASURED ONE. Every integration in this repo was unit-tested and green while the product was broken: Indico's verifier reported 6/6 for months from Node, where neither CSP nor CORS is enforced, so it could not see that no browser had ever reached the server. Single-integration tests answer 'does the client work'; only a crossing scenario answers 'does the user's sentence work'. Scenarios must therefore run at the layer the user actually stands on — a real browser, real servers — or they will repeat the same lie in a new place." ;
