## -- F126-F128 + repo-scan refinements (2026-08-13) -----------------------------
## Two features SHIPPED this session and are recorded here as functional; the rest are
## refinements drawn from an external repository scan (11 repos, reviewed by Opus).
## Every claim below was measured, not assumed — where a thing is NOT built, it says so.

kb:merge-synonyms rdf:type ktype:Feature ;
               kpred:touches-module code:rdf ;
    kpred:actual-files "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    kpred:actual-deps "0"^^xsd:integer ;
               rdfs:label   "Synonyms survive a merge" ;
               kpred:feature-id   "F126" ;
               kpred:has-status   "functional" ;
               kpred:priority     "high" ;
               kpred:relates-to   kb:entity-normalization ;
               kpred:relates-to   kb:entity-sets ;
               kpred:tested-by    "src/lib/rdf/__tests__/merge-aliases.test.ts" ;
               kpred:description  "Matt (2026-08-13): 'we need some way to track all synonyms within a node. When merging multiple nodes into one that list should automatically occur.' Merging now preserves every name the merged entities answered to, as skos:altLabel on the surviving node, automatically and without a review step." ;
               kpred:evidence     "THE BUG WAS LOSSY AND SILENT. src/routes/(app)/review/+page.svelte redirects the dropped entity's statements onto the kept one, and MergeReview.svelte classifies two different rdfs:label values as a CONFLICT whose loser is set to 'rejected' (default resolution is 'a'). So merging 'Ava Farmers Market' into 'Ava Growers Market' destroyed the first name — the very name a source used, a search would look for, and the next import will arrive as, at which point the entity duplicates again and a human merges it a second time." ;
               kpred:decided      "skos:altLabel, NOT A NEW PREDICATE. SKOS is already this project's vocabulary for concept relations (skos:broader and skos:narrower drive rdf/hierarchy.ts; skos:definition appears in ghost-graph.ts and dichotomy.ts) and altLabel is SKOS's own term for alternate lexical labels beside a single preferred one. Minting kpred:synonym would be the private-vocabulary mistake graph-lint already warns about — 73 of 315 predicates used exactly once — and would not survive export to any other tool." ;
               kpred:principle    "A MERGE IS A CLAIM THAT TWO NAMES DENOTE ONE THING, so discarding the losing name throws away the evidence for the claim being made. It is a lossy edit dressed as a cleanup." ;
               kpred:decided      "THE LOSING NAME IS PRESERVED WHICHEVER SIDE LOSES. If the user resolves the label conflict in favour of the DROPPED entity, the KEPT entity's original name is the one about to be rejected — so the alias pass reads the surviving primary label and preserves everything else, rather than assuming the kept entity's name always wins. Tested explicitly." ;
               kpred:evidence     "TRANSITIVITY IS FREE, and that is why this is a statement rather than a side table. Aliases are statements whose subject is the kept entity, so a later merge of that entity into a third redirects them along with everything else. A node merged three times still carries every name it has ever had, with no special handling." ;
               kpred:remaining    "BUILT: src/lib/rdf/merge-aliases.ts (pure — value derivation, case/whitespace normalisation, dedupe, IRI-slug recovery, primary-label resolution) wired into onMergeConfirm, 12 tests. NOT BUILT: search does not yet match an entity by its altLabel, and the node panel does not display or let you edit the synonym list. entityAnswersTo() exists for the first of those and has no caller." .

kb:import-target-resolution rdf:type ktype:Feature ;
               kpred:touches-module code:storage ;
    kpred:actual-files "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    kpred:actual-deps "0"^^xsd:integer ;
               rdfs:label   "Re-importing a graph updates it instead of duplicating it" ;
               kpred:feature-id   "F127" ;
               kpred:has-status   "functional" ;
               kpred:priority     "high" ;
               kpred:relates-to   kb:multi-kb ;
               kpred:relates-to   kb:graph-sets ;
               kpred:tested-by    "src/lib/storage/__tests__/kb-import-target.test.ts" ;
               kpred:description  "One shared rule deciding where an imported graph lands: replace an existing graph, ask the user, or create a new one. Removes the cause of duplicated graph names rather than only reporting them." ;
               kpred:evidence     "MEASURED 2026-08-13 in Matt's own registry: FIVE duplicated names (reckons-production, reckons-roadmap, starter-everyday, starter-quickstart, starter-visual-review), each covering more than one independent copy, several never opened. Three of the four import paths already resolved a target correctly — drive-sync matches stableId then name, workspace import skips known names and stableIds, the docs-leap path reuses a found entry — while the FILE IMPORT at src/routes/(app)/ingest/+page.svelte called createKb() with no registry check of any kind. The duplicated names are exactly static/*.ttl filenames minus their extension, which is what that page derives a name from." ;
               kpred:decided      "THE TWO SIGNALS ARE NOT EQUALLY STRONG, and conflating them is how an import destroys work. A STABLE ID match means 'this IS that graph, newer' — replacing in place is correct, and ingestExistingKb takes a recovery snapshot first. A NAME match means 'possibly the same graph': 'roadmap.ttl' from two different projects collides trivially, so a name match warns and offers the choice, and the SAFE branch (keep both, suffixed readably) is the default. Overwriting on a name match would be a data-loss bug dressed as deduplication." ;
               kpred:constraint   "REPLACING MUST ACTUALLY REPLACE. The ingest path wrote into an existing database without clearing it first, so a replace would have left old facts beside new ones and silently doubled the graph. statements and sources are now cleared inside the replace branch." ;
               kpred:remaining    "BUILT: src/lib/storage/kb-import-target.ts (resolveImportTarget, uniqueKbName), 11 tests, wired into the ingest file-import path, which now also reports 'Updated' rather than 'Created' when it replaced. NOT BUILT: the five EXISTING duplicate pairs are untouched — the graphs page still only reports them, and which copy is real remains a judgement about content that no heuristic should make. A merge-or-discard affordance on that notice is the follow-up." .

kb:shape-validation rdf:type ktype:Feature ;
               kpred:touches-module code:rdf ;
    kpred:actual-files "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    kpred:actual-deps "2"^^xsd:integer ;
