    kpred:description "Settles the F59 open question Matt left UNDECIDED, and fixes the 'starter-graph timeline force still looks bad' item carried in HANDOFF since 2026-07-31. In event mode a node with no recognised temporal predicate now goes to a labelled UNDATED LANE below the axis instead of being placed at its statement's createdAt." ;
    kpred:evidence "THE BUG WAS BIGGER THAN A COSMETIC ONE, and it is measured. Both renderers fell back to createdAt — the INGESTION time — for undated nodes and placed them as if that were an event. On starter-everyday.ttl only 12 of 177 nodes carry a date, so 93% were placed by import time; starter-guide.ttl has 216 nodes and NOT ONE date, so 100% were. Worse than the resulting wall of nodes: those fake timestamps entered dataMin/dataMax, so the axis spanned 36 days and the real 4-day trip was compressed into 11.1% of it. Measured in the running app against the real graph." ;
    kpred:evidence "THE LANE WAS ALREADY WRITTEN AND UNREACHABLE. Both renderers contained an else-branch placing undated nodes at y = -SPREAD_Y * 0.7 — dead code, because the createdAt fallback guaranteed every node received a time and the branch never ran. The fix largely made the existing intent actually happen." ;
    kpred:decided "MATT, 2026-08-13: the undated lane, over hiding undated nodes entirely (93% of the starter graph would vanish on switching layout) and over keeping them placed while fixing only the range (the wall remains, still claiming a date it does not have). Placing an undated node at its ingestion time is the graph asserting a date it does not have, in the one view whose entire job is to say when things happened." ;
    kpred:known-issue "THREE FURTHER DEFECTS FOUND IN THE SAME CODE AND FIXED. (1) In 3D, `if (useIngested) A else if (!useIngested) A` — byte-identical branches reading as though they distinguished cases. (2) In 2D, getTimelineDataRange (which bounds the right-click scrub) EXCLUDED the createdAt fallback while buildTimelineAnchors2D INCLUDED it, so the scrub bounds and the node positions disagreed and dragging felt broken. (3) The recognised temporal predicates existed in THREE copies — KnowledgeGraph, KnowledgeGraph2D and parse-date.ts — which is the drift parse-date.ts's own comment exists to prevent; all now read the one set." ;
    kpred:remaining "BUILT: src/lib/rdf/timeline-layout.ts (buildNodeTimes, timelineRange, undatedCount), 14 tests, both renderers wired to it, lane spread over 5 rows clear of the dated band and labelled 'no date (N)'. NOT DONE: the camera does not auto-fit the axis plus lane, so the layout needs a manual zoom-out to see whole; and 165 parked nodes remain inherently dense — clustering or collapsing the lane is a further step." .

