    kpred:decided "AN ESTIMATE IS NEVER BACK-FILLED ONTO FINISHED WORK. estimated-* and actual-* are separate predicates precisely so the two cannot be confused: an 'estimate' written after the fact is not a prediction, and scoring one would make every calibration figure a lie. scope-check --calibration therefore reports that estimate quality is UNKNOWN — zero designs carry both — and says why, rather than manufacturing a flattering number from six retrofitted guesses." ;
    kpred:known-issue "THE IN-FLIGHT CHECK OVER-COUNTS ON A MIXED BRANCH, and the first real run proved it: against a branch carrying five unrelated concerns it reported 39 source files against every estimate, so F75's 5-file estimate appeared to be over by 34. git diff cannot attribute a file to a feature. The report prints this caveat rather than hiding it, and the real remedy is one branch per feature — which this working tree is currently a counter-example to." ;
    kpred:remaining "BUILT: the estimate vocabulary (kpred:estimated-files / estimated-deps / actual-files / actual-deps) validated by SHACL as non-negative integers; scripts/offline/scope-check.ts in both calibration and in-flight modes, registered in the offline suite, never failing a build. NOT BUILT: no task records OBSERVATIONS DURING implementation, so creepSeries and the gradual-vs-step distinction are still unexercised by real data — the series needs a harness taking readings as it works, which is F87. And estimate quality stays unknown until one of the three estimated features is actually built." .

