    kpred:description "New 2026-08-12 3.1B multimodal release: an LFM2.5 2.6B language backbone plus a 400M SigLIP2 NaFlex vision encoder, with official GGUF, ONNX/WebGPU, MLX, Transformers, llama.cpp, Ollama, vLLM and SGLang paths. It is optimized for short direct visual work, screen grounding, multi-image input and OCR/layout rather than long visual-design reasoning. This is a MODEL CANDIDATE inside F31/F70.2/F74.6, not a new Reckons feature and not a default merely because vendor benchmarks are strong." ;
    kpred:measurement "REPO GATE, 2026-08-17. Official Q4_K_M plus Q8 projector was pulled through Ollama as hf.co/LiquidAI/LFM2.5-VL-3B-GGUF:Q4_K_M (local Ollama id 3e9bb91d3103, 2.3 GB). On the existing 10-screenshot / 48-check / num_ctx=8192 gate it scored 38/48 = 79.2%, ZERO false-negative misses, 10 false flags, p50 769 ms and p95 1262 ms in 42.1 s. Evidence: tests/visual/results/vlm-gate_2026-08-17T16-16-10.json." ;
    kpred:measurement "SAME-SESSION QWEN CONTROL, 2026-08-17. qwen2.5vl:7b scored 44/48 = 91.7%, one dangerous miss, three false flags, p50 537 ms and p95 1157 ms in 42.3 s. Evidence: tests/visual/results/vlm-gate_2026-08-17T16-17-15.json. The older July run was 45/48 with zero misses, so one run does not establish a stable recall winner." ;
    kpred:measurement "PRODUCTION TWO-IMAGE SMOKE, 2026-08-17. Through the exact diffImagesVLM /api/generate path, both models called one duplicated screenshot IDENTICAL. Given two plainly different Reckons app views in BOTH orders, LFM2.5-VL-3B returned CHANGED both times with concrete header/layout differences. qwen2.5vl:7b called the forward pair IDENTICAL, then called the reversed pair CHANGED with partly invented node differences — direct evidence of image-order instability on this pair. This is one pair, not a benchmark, but it blocks a single global winner assumption and makes Liquid the leading candidate for the pairwise-diff role." ;
    kpred:note "USER OBSERVATION, Matt 2026-08-17: LFM2.5-VL-3B looked very good at multi-image work. Preserve this as attributed qualitative evidence alongside the measured pair smoke, not as a promotion verdict; the labelled pair corpus must determine whether the impression generalizes." ;
    kpred:note "DISCOVERY WARNING. Ordinary web/model indexes initially surfaced only LFM2-VL-3B and the older 1.6B/450M LFM2.5-VL models because this release was six days old. The live Hugging Face API returned LiquidAI/LFM2.5-VL-3B (created 2026-08-11) and its official artifacts. Future model audits must query the publisher API/model registry directly before concluding an exact new model does not exist." ;
    kpred:decided "ROUTE BY MEASURED VISUAL ROLE, NOT ONE MODEL NAME. Keep qwen2.5vl:7b as the current single-image presence-gate default until replicated evidence says otherwise. Build a labelled two-image corpus before selecting the visual-diff model; let F74.6 record the role, exact artifact/version and validation result. A 2.3 GB model that raises more harmless false alarms may still be the better cheap lane when zero misses or GPU co-residency matters." ;
    kpred:constraint "LICENSE AND ARTIFACT IDENTITY ARE ROUTING INPUTS. Do not bundle, silently download or make this the universal default without exposing the LFM license boundary. Record quantization, language/projector artifact, Ollama/model digest, context and corpus revision; a mutable Hugging Face tag is not reproducible evidence." ;
    kpred:honest-note "CONTEXT METADATA DISAGREES. The release model card says 32,768 context while config/GGUF/Ollama metadata advertise 128,000. Treat 32K as the documented support claim until tested. Reckons pins 8,192, so this discrepancy does not affect the recorded runs." ;
    kpred:remaining "Before routing changes: three repeated gate runs; a labelled identical/harmless/meaningful two-image corpus in both image orders; strict visual-evidence JSON/schema compliance; OCR/layout fixtures under F70.2; Q4_K_M versus Q8/BF16 quality ceiling; peak VRAM/power and concurrency-one/two measurements including co-residency with qwen3-coder. Adoption gate: parseable output, no worse pairwise false-negative rate than the incumbent, and either incumbent-level accuracy or a measured memory/concurrency win." .

