    kpred:description "A young open specification and pair of Python reference converters for treating each Markdown note as one RDF subject: YAML-LD frontmatter supplies predicate/object facts, Obsidian wiki links supply IRI edges, composed external context.jsonld files supply terms and scoped bases, and prose bodies remain outside the triple set. It can generate schema.ttl/data.ttl from a vault and generate/update a vault from RDF. Useful ideas include explicit source-of-truth direction, vld:path placement fidelity, deterministic no-op regeneration, composed-context collision warnings and strong untrusted-vault path/frontmatter tests." ;
    kpred:measurement "UPSTREAM CHECK, 2026-08-17. At v0.5.0 the 31 security tests pass and the bundled 11-subject/44-triple example round-trips graph-isomorphically. The project has no database, query engine, manifest, revisions, locking, atomic multi-file promotion, conflict handling or sync protocol; unsupported fidelity cases generally warn rather than fail." ;
    kpred:measurement "DECISIVE RECKONS INCOMPATIBILITY, reproduced 2026-08-17. The reference tools accept an explicit id only for http(s). A minimal RDF -> vault -> RDF probe changed urn:kbase:concept/x into https://example.org/data/urn:kbase:concept/x and rebased URN types and predicates too. A separate minimal @vocab fixture did not follow the spec's compatibility profile: type: concept was based under @base and an unmapped custom field was skipped." ;
    kpred:decided "REFERENCE AND CONFORMANCE SPIKE ONLY — NO STORAGE/SYNC ADAPTER YET. Vault-LD may become an optional generated Markdown/interchange VIEW after exact-IRI and loss-boundary fixtures pass. It cannot replace Dexie, the F107.3 canonical graph package, TriG source provenance, workspace sync, graph sets or MCP storage. Reckons remains graph-first; a generated Vault-LD tree is never an authoritative backup." ;
    kpred:constraint "CURRENT NO-GO FOR AUTHORITATIVE INTERCHANGE. Every urn:kbase subject, predicate, type and IRI object must round-trip exactly before any user graph enters this path. Review statuses, statement identity, sources/named graphs, extraction/changelog links, stable graph ids, revisions, assets, pending inbox and graph-set roles must remain in the canonical package rather than being projected away." ;
    kpred:constraint "IMPORT IS A STAGED TRANSACTION OR IT DOES NOT TOUCH LIVE STATE. Blank nodes, language tags, named graphs, RDF-star, unsupported SHACL, ambiguous wiki links, malformed/oversized contexts, remote contexts, cancellation, concurrent runs and mid-write failure must either map losslessly or hard-fail before promotion; stderr warnings and partial file rewrites are not acceptance." ;
    kpred:honest-note "Reckons' current JSON-LD function is a confirmed/refined Schema.org PUBLISHING VIEW, not a lossless RDF dataset importer or backup format. Do not route Vault-LD through semantic-export.ts or describe folder-scan reading .jsonld as JSON-LD support." ;
    kpred:remaining "Bounded spike only if interoperability is desired: pin the upstream tag; run exact URN/@vocab/context-collision/identity fixtures; round-trip the clean supported subset of the MCP-visible corpus; preserve bodies and host keys; prove a second conversion changes zero files; define deletion/tombstones; stage then atomically promote; reuse the upstream security suite; benchmark 10k/100k triples. If exact identity or hard loss accounting fails, retain only the security/profile lessons and add no permanent adapter feature." .

